  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"2.16\"\n\nrecipe:\n  name: \"looptools\"\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://feynarts.de/looptools/LoopTools-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 4113467575db3a14405d62d9e516b3b90410b73ea8d20c8eb8d70a30fc5cc9cb\n  patches:\n    - use-STRIP-from-the-environment.patch\n    - link-the-Fortran-runtime-by-name.patch\n    - link-the-REAL-16-check-with-LDFLAGS.patch\n    - pass-all-five-point-arguments-from-EgetC.patch\n    - use-the-Cxx-compiler-when-called-as-fxx.patch\n    - do-not-add-stdlib-libstdc-when-MathLink-is-not-found.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 7\n  skip: win\n\noutputs:\n  - package:\n      name: \"looptools-static\"\n    build:\n      script:\n        - ./configure --help\n        # Author has disabled builds with dynamic linking\n        # c.f. https://github.com/hep-packaging-coordination/packaging-hep-simulation-stack/issues/4#issuecomment-2489198926\n        - ./configure --prefix=$PREFIX\n        # configure sets PARALLEL to use every core on the machine and\n        # LIBDIRSUFFIX to install to $PREFIX/lib64 on x86_64 and ppc64le\n        - make install PARALLEL=\"-j${CPU_COUNT}\" LIBDIRSUFFIX=\n        # The compilers fcc calls are run requirements, so are found under $PREFIX\n        # and not $BUILD_PREFIX at install time.\n        - sed -i \"s|$BUILD_PREFIX|$PREFIX|g\" $PREFIX/bin/fcc\n    requirements:\n      build:\n        - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n        - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n        - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n        - ${{ compiler('fortran') }}\n        - make\n        - sed\n      run:\n        # fcc requires the existence of a C and C++ compiler to work\n        - if: linux\n          then: gxx\n        - if: osx\n          then: clangxx\n\n    tests:\n      - package_contents:\n          strict: true\n          bin:\n            - lt\n            - fcc\n            - f++\n          include:\n            - looptools.h\n            - clooptools.h\n          files:\n            - lib/libooptools.a\n            - etc/conda/test-files/*\n\n      - files:\n          recipe:\n            - examples/\n        requirements:\n          run:\n            - grep\n        script:\n          - lt 1\n          # The three-, four-, and five-point tensor coefficients use REAL*16\n          - lt 1000 2000 9000 100 200 300\n          - lt 100 200 300 400 5000 -2000 10 20 30 40\n          - lt 0 0 0 0 0 250000 -12239.172 150000 25000 -31183.285 10000 10000 10000 10000 10000\n          # configure falls back to double precision without an error if its\n          # check for REAL*16 fails\n          - grep -e \"-DQUADSIZE=16\" $PREFIX/bin/fcc\n          # configure adds -stdlib=libstdc++ to the C++ compiler flags of fcc\n          # if its check for MathLink is left unpatched, which is wrong for macOS\n          - if grep -e \"-stdlib=libstdc++\" $PREFIX/bin/fcc; then exit 1; fi\n          - fcc --help\n          - f++ --help\n\n          # The compilers in the run requirements do not set any environment\n          # variables on activation\n          - export CXX=${{ \"g++\" if linux else \"clang++\" }}\n          - export CXXFLAGS=\"-I$PREFIX/include\"\n          - export LDFLAGS=\"-L$PREFIX/lib -Wl,-rpath,$PREFIX/lib\"\n\n          - cd examples\n          - $CXX example01.cpp -o example01 $CXXFLAGS $LDFLAGS -looptools -lgfortran\n          - ./example01\n          - fcc example01.cpp -o example01-fcc -looptools\n          - ./example01-fcc\n          - fcc example02.c -o example02 -looptools\n          - ./example02\n          # example03 needs the C++ standard library, so links only if the C++\n          # compiler is used. f++ uses it for any source file and fcc only for\n          # a source file with the .cc extension.\n          - f++ example03.cpp -o example03 -looptools\n          - ./example03\n          - cp example03.cpp example03.cc\n          - fcc example03.cc -o example03-fcc -looptools\n          - ./example03-fcc\n          # libooptools.a is linked into shared libraries by downstream packages,\n          # so it must be position independent\n          - $CXX -shared -fPIC example01.cpp -o libexample01.so $CXXFLAGS $LDFLAGS -looptools -lgfortran\n\nabout:\n  summary: \"LoopTools: A package for evaluation of scalar and tensor one-loop integrals\"\n  description: |\n    LoopTools is a package for evaluation of scalar and tensor one-loop integrals\n    based on the FF package by G.J. van Oldenborgh. It features an easy Fortran,\n    C++, and Mathematica interface to the scalar one-loop functions of FF and\n    in addition provides the 2-, 3-, and 4-point tensor coefficient functions.\n\n    The [publication](https://inspirehep.net/literature/474106) associated with\n    LoopTools is: T. Hahn, M. Pérez-Victoria. Automated one-loop calculations\n    in four and D dimensions, _Comput. Phys. Commun._ 118 (1999) 153.\n    DOI: [10.1016/S0010-4655(98)00173-8](https://doi.org/10.1016/S0010-4655(98)00173-8)\n  license: LGPL-3.0-only\n  license_file: COPYING\n  homepage: https://feynarts.de/looptools/\n\nextra:\n  feedstock-name: looptools\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - matthewfeickert\n",
